# The X session, for the Handles tab's profile and followings.
#
# Everything here is optional. Without it the dashboard runs, indexes the chain
# and answers every tab except the two that reach X, which return 503 with the
# reason. Nothing in this file is read by any other part of the server.
#
# Copy to .env beside the X client you point at with PONS_XCLIENT_DIR, or
# export the same names in the environment.

# The auth token of the account the dashboard reads X as. Required for the two
# X endpoints. Never logged: xsource.py prints the variable's name, never its
# value.
AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional, only if you keep several accounts. PARSE_ACCOUNTS is the comma
# separated list of labels, and each label gets its own AUTH_TOKEN_<LABEL>,
# uppercase with dashes turned into underscores. An unlabelled AUTH_TOKEN
# above still works as the fallback.
# PARSE_ACCOUNTS=main,reader
# AUTH_TOKEN_MAIN=
# AUTH_TOKEN_READER=

# Optional outbound proxy for the X requests only.
# PROXY=
